{
  "class": "ParticlePacket",
  "module": "server/play/particle_packet",
  "module_docs": [
    "Port of `net.minestom.server.network.packet.server.play.ParticlePacket`.",
    "",
    "# Deferrals",
    "",
    "**None.** The particle goes out through the ported",
    "`crate::particle::network_type()` \u2014 `Particle.NETWORK_TYPE`, the var-int id",
    "*and* the variant's `writeData` \u2014 so a `Particle.Block` carries its block",
    "state id and a `Particle.Dust` its colour and scale.",
    "`probes/expected/particlewireprobe.json` pins both a data-free",
    "`Particle.Simple` and a data-carrying `Particle.Block` through this",
    "serializer.",
    "",
    "Java's four convenience constructors (`maxSpeed` broadcast to three axes,",
    "`Point` overloads, `Randomization.DEFAULT`) are ported as `new_with_*`",
    "helpers, since Rust has no constructor overloading."
  ],
